// Who Everglade's people are, as words (eg-people; #13261): their names, roles, greetings and what
// they know of the city, and the city's controls. The page (people.coax, which loads this) and the
// server (coax/web/api/npc-personas.coax, which loads it too) read the same constants, so the persona
// the server gives the model and the one the page shows can't drift. A page sends only a person's id
// (verse/talk-id.coax of their name); the server looks them up here.
//   coax/bin/coax test verse/everglade/people-words.coax --library
#load "../talk-id.coax";

EG_PEOPLE :: 28;   // plan.coax's EG_SPOTS (people.coax checks the two agree)
EG_WORLD :: "Everglade";
EG_WORLD_ID :: "everglade";   // the world, as a page names it to the server
// The city's controls, for a character asked how to do something.
EG_CONTROLS :: "W A S D or the arrows move you at a run, Shift walks, Space jumps, drag the mouse to look, the wheel zooms, M shows the city from above; on a phone the left thumb walks and the right looks. Walk up to someone and press E, or tap TALK, to talk to them; type and press Enter to say something, and Esc or BYE ends it. Players can't build or change the city.";

